{"availability":"available","full":"GabriellyFerreiraa/payload-cms-demo","name":"payload-cms-demo","description":"Headless CMS inside a Next.js App Router app — content authored in Payload, stored in Postgres, rendered by Server Components. No API token in the render path.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-17T19:46:26Z","updated":"2026-09-19T11:48:41Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://payload-cms-demo-sigma.vercel.app","topics":["headless-cms","nextjs","payload-cms","postgresql","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://payload-cms-demo-sigma.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:08:55.704Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T02:08:55.704Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T02:08:55.704Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:08:19.180Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T02:08:55.704Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Note: This is a focused demo, not a client project. Built to work through how Payload CMS sits inside a Next.js App Router application — where the server boundary falls, and what changes when the CMS is a dependency instead of a separate service. See Why build this? below.","Most \"headless CMS\" setups are two systems: a CMS somewhere else, and a frontend that fetches from it over HTTP. That means an API token to protect, a network hop on every render, and CORS to configure.","Payload works differently. It's a dependency of the Next.js app, not a service next to it. The admin panel is a route in the same application, and content is read through a Local API that queries the database directly on the server."],"features":["Content model as code — the posts collection is a TypeScript config file, so schema changes are reviewable in a pull request and versioned like any other code.","Local API rendering — payload.find() queries Postgres directly from a Server Component. No HTTP round trip, no API token in the render path.","Draft/published states — the public query filters on status, so unpublished work is never rendered.","Rich text authoring — content is stored as structured JSON rather than an HTML blob, so it can be rendered differently per surface.","Credentials server-side only — DATABASEURL and PAYLOADSECRET are set as Vercel environment variables and carry no NEXTPUBLIC prefix, so they never enter the client bundle."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GabriellyFerreiraa/payload-cms-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"399874816f71ae32b186152142646c4386bba6198c702b1d14400e0efccdcf89","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T16:08:19.329Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:08:19.329Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Note: This is a focused demo, not a client project. Built to work through how Payload CMS sits inside a Next.js App Router application — where the server boundary falls, and what changes when the CMS is a dependency instead of a separate service. See Why build this? below.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GabriellyFerreiraa/payload-cms-demo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"399874816f71ae32b186152142646c4386bba6198c702b1d14400e0efccdcf89","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GabriellyFerreiraa/payload-cms-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T16:08:19.329Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-19T11:48:41Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GabriellyFerreiraa/payload-cms-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T16:08:19.330Z","hash":"399874816f71ae32b186152142646c4386bba6198c702b1d14400e0efccdcf89","originalBytes":9152,"storedBytes":9152,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["payload","cms","admin","api","app","content","panel","postgres","que","secret","database","public","como","next.js","next","token","typescript","blica","npm","server","url","vercel","del","frontend","local","request","router","status","string","changes","connection","consulta","